{"id":"code-merge-intervals","title":"Merge overlapping intervals","category":"code","difficulty":2,"prompt":"Write a Python function `merge_intervals(intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]`. Each interval is `[start, end]` with start <= end. Return the merged intervals sorted by start. Intervals that overlap or touch (one ends where the next begins) are merged. The input may be in any order and must not be modified.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"merge_intervals","tests":["assert merge_intervals([]) == []","assert merge_intervals([[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]) == [[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]","assert merge_intervals([[8, 10], [1, 3], [2, 6]]) == [[1, 6], [8, 10]]","assert merge_intervals([[1, 2], [2, 3]]) == [[1, 3]]","assert merge_intervals([[1, 10], [2, 3], [4, 5]]) == [[1, 10]]","assert merge_intervals([[5, 5], [1, 1]]) == [[1, 1], [5, 5]]","x = [[4, 6], [1, 5]]; merge_intervals(x); assert x == [[4, 6], [1, 5]]"]},"reference":"```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    merged: list[list[int]] = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals):\n        if merged and start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n```","answers":["```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    merged: list[list[int]] = []\n    for start, end in intervals:\n        if merged and start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n```","```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    merged: list[list[int]] = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals):\n        if merged and start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.71428571,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":7,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.175,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":171,"output_tokens":329,"cost_usd":0.0001816,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.71428571,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":7,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.175,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":171,"output_tokens":180,"cost_usd":0.0001071,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":2,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.71428571,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":7,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.175,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":171,"output_tokens":199,"cost_usd":0.0001166,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-medium","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.71428571,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":7,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.377,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":171,"output_tokens":525,"cost_usd":0.0002796,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-medium","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","sc